[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   Step 071 -- radial slip profile: where does the anomalous rotation
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   accumulate?
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   The step-063 bidirectional legs are extended to a set of boundary shells
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   (60-400 AU).  On each leg the osculating barycentric periapsis direction
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   is recorded at every shell crossing, so the inbound/outbound rotation
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   delta_theta(s) is measured as a function of radius rather than only at
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   250 AU.  For a discrete phase slip applied at a crossing radius r*,
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   delta_theta(s) is flat inside r* (baseline only) and offsets by the slip
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   angle for s > r* -- the kink radius localizes the boundary; for a
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   distributed field delta_theta(s) grows continuously.  The implied
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   proper-time profile delta_tau(s) = delta_theta(s) * s^2 / h converts
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   each shell measurement to time units.
[2026-09-21 14:48:15 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 071]   Outputs:
